(12251, 5, '2025-08-08 13:35:59', '2025-08-08 17:35:59', 'This image titled "Idea Phase" features an icon of a blueprint and pencil on a dark green background, symbolizing early-stage planning. On the right, text describes the ideal team member traits for this phase: adaptable creatives and marketers with broad skills who excel with feedback and change, strong problem-solvers in resource-limited settings, and independent, flexible communicators who are comfortable with risk. This visual supports Sandy’s blog post on building the right team for a growing business by highlighting the qualities essential during a company\'s early planning stage.', 'Idea Phase', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'idea-phase', '', '', '2025-08-08 13:38:35', '2025-08-08 17:38:35', '', 12128, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Idea-Phase.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12252, 5, '2025-08-08 13:39:37', '2025-08-08 17:39:37', 'This “Build Phase” graphic shows an icon of a building under construction on a dark navy background, symbolizing the growth and structuring stage of a business. On the right, descriptive text highlights ideal team member qualities: resourceful builders experienced in developing systems, teams, and processes; collaborative problem-solvers; and strategic communicators who learn quickly and drive progress. The visual complements Sandy’s blog on building the right team by outlining the key traits needed as businesses transition from early-stage ideas to scalable execution.', 'Build Phase', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'build-phase', '', '', '2025-08-08 13:41:09', '2025-08-08 17:41:09', '', 12128, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Build-Phase.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12253, 5, '2025-08-08 13:41:35', '2025-08-08 17:41:35', 'This “Scale Phase” visual features a light pink background with a white icon of multiple buildings, symbolizing an organization entering a mature, growth-focused stage. On the right, text outlines the ideal team profile: strategic thinkers who craft long-term plans, bring leadership experience, and excel in building culture within large teams. Their work style is growth-minded and efficient, emphasizing team development. This image supports Sandy’s blog about building the right team for your growing business by identifying the key capabilities needed during scaling.', 'Scale Phase', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'scale-phase', '', '', '2025-08-08 13:43:28', '2025-08-08 17:43:28', '', 12128, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Scale-Phase.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12254, 5, '2025-08-08 13:43:51', '2025-08-08 17:43:51', 'This “Established Phase” image features a purple background with a white outline of multiple office buildings surrounded by trees, radiating lines suggesting maturity and stability. On the right, the accompanying text defines the ideal team persona: seasoned leaders experienced in managing major business transitions. They are skilled in building top-tier teams, especially from enterprise environments, and bring a systems-oriented, proactive approach with a focus on long-term, scalable growth. The image supports Sandy’s blog about aligning team capabilities with different business stages.', 'Established Phase', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'established-phase', '', '', '2025-08-08 13:44:53', '2025-08-08 17:44:53', '', 12128, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Established-Phase.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12255, 5, '2025-08-08 13:46:21', '2025-08-08 17:46:21', '<span style="font-weight: 400;">As a startup leader, I spend a lot of time reading and learning from others who are on a similar journey. It\'s fascinating – and reassuring – to learn how common the challenges we face are, despite often feeling unique to our business or industry. This shared journey highlights the common hurdles every business encounters.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">One of the most significant hurdles is hiring the right people. This challenge isn\'t exclusive to startups; it\'s critical for any business. However, the specific needs in terms of talent can vary dramatically at various stages of a business\'s growth.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">I recently read a book by Dave Hersh called "Reignition," which had an interesting section about the risks of hiring the wrong team. A business evolves through many stages: from the idea, to the build phase, to scaling up, and finally becoming an established, profitable business. As we navigate the space between these phases, edging toward the next milestone, we can usually identify where we currently sit, but where we often fail is recognizing the types of talent we need based on where the business is to move us to that next phase.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">For all of us, the nightmare scenario is hiring the wrong person. Even more daunting is the prospect of retaining a poor fit. I\'m sure many founders can relate. The cost of a bad hire is significant, with estimates suggesting a financial impact of at least 30% of the employee’s annual salary. This doesn\'t even account for the time lost managing underperformers – approximately a day per week – and up to 40% of time diverted into recruiting and training replacements. These figures are conservative; the impact on a small, agile startup team is typically much more severe.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Often, there\'s a period of denial where we convince ourselves the hire might not be as bad as we think, attributing issues to imperfection. However, frustration mounts as performance continues to fall short, and soon the entire team notices. By the time you decide to address the issue, you’re deep into managing the fallout, which includes difficult conversations, notice periods, and realigning with HR - assuming you have such a department. The frustration of navigating this process can be overwhelming, along with the realization that you should have taken action sooner.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s incredibly draining, saps the company of crucial resources including time, attention, emotional energy, and financial resources, as well as potential payouts for contract settlements. And then, there’s the challenge of rebooting the recruitment and hiring process again.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Hopefully, each hiring challenge should help refine your approach, aligning future hires more closely with your company’s culture and needs. However, it’s important to remember, cultural fit is only one aspect. A clear view of the current business environment and your specific needs is crucial for effective talent acquisition. As Dave points out in his book, Reignition, ‘while loyalty is admirable, it’s useless if it leads to a stalled venture’. The right team for the right time is essential to navigate market trends, product development, and channel strategies amid uncertainties. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">So, what does all this mean when it comes to finding the right talent for where your business is now? While it’s tempting to think that seasoned talent from larger, established brands would be a perfect fit, it might not be the right time for that just yet. On the flip side, the jack-of-all-trades creative lead who helped you navigate your early growth phase might not be the best match as you begin to scale. It’s all about aligning talent with your current stage and future goals.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">To help guide you, we’ve put together a few scenarios based on common business stages. While every situation is unique and talent can grow alongside your business, these scenarios provide a practical framework to shape your talent strategy and keep it aligned with your growth goals.</span>\r\n\r\n<b>Idea Phase: </b><span style="font-weight: 400;">You\'re actively testing and tweaking your product offerings to nail the perfect product-market fit.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12251" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Idea-Phase-1024x636.png" alt="Idea Phase team traits – adaptable creatives, problem solvers, and proactive marketers ideal for early-stage business growth" width="1024" height="636" />\r\n\r\n<b>Build Phase:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You\'re focused on increasing revenue and fine-tuning your business model, refining everything from sales strategies and distribution channels to market positioning and product offerings.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12252" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Build-Phase-1024x636.png" alt="Build Phase team traits – resourceful builders, collaborative problem-solvers, and fast-learning communicators ideal for scaling systems and teams." width="1024" height="636" />\r\n\r\n<b>Scale Phase:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You\'re committed to building a long-term infrastructure that supports growth, tailored to market demands and your unique strengths. At the same time, you\'re exploring opportunities to capture a larger market share. This stage also demands specialized skills in areas like creative, brand, digital marketing and data analytics. </span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12253" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Scale-Phase-1024x638.png" alt="Scale Phase team traits – strategic thinkers with leadership experience, focused on long-term planning, team growth, and organizational culture." width="1024" height="638" />\r\n\r\n<b>Established Phase:</b><span style="font-weight: 400;"> You\'re well established with a strong market presence and stable revenue streams. You\'re exploring new avenues for expansion, seeking acquisition opportunities that resonate with your product or mission, and streamlining the company to maximize profitability.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12254" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/02/Established-Phase-1024x636.png" alt="Established Phase team traits – strategic leaders with enterprise experience focused on scalable growth and complex business challenges." width="1024" height="636" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">No matter where your business is in its journey, nothing is more impactful than having the right team at the right time. It starts with a clear understanding of your business stage, clearly defining roles and expectations, thoroughly evaluating candidates, and strong alignment with your company\'s culture and strategic objectives.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">At Sandy, we connect exceptional creative and marketing talent with forward-thinking organizations, offering flexible resource solutions that help teams thrive in today\'s dynamic workplace. By streamlining processes and delivering the right talent at the right time, we can help you improve productivity while providing a cost-effective alternative to full-time hires.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">If any of this resonates, we’d love to hear from you! Please feel free to <a href="https://worksandy.com/find-talent/">reach out</a>, we’d be happy to share our expertise and help you tackle the challenges of building a top performing team to support your business growth. </span>', 'Building the Right Team for Your Growing Business', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '12128-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-08-08 13:46:21', '2025-08-08 17:46:21', '', 12128, 'https://worksandy.com/?p=12255', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(12256, 5, '2025-08-14 19:46:07', '2025-08-14 23:46:07', '<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ve all been there.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The team’s underwater, deadlines are looming, and Slack has taken on a tone of panic. You know it’s time to bring in help - but by the time you do, things are already on fire.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">So you start scrambling - pinging old contacts, texting friends-of-friends, chasing down leads like your next deliverable depends on it (because, well, it does). You finally land someone great, rush through contracts, toss them an NDA, and then… throw them in the deep end.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s a familiar move: hiring out of urgency, not strategy. And while it might get you across the finish line, it rarely sets your new hire - or your team - up for long-term success.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The good news? There’s a better way. One that makes bringing in the right support faster, easier, and actually effective. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Let’s talk about moving from reactive hiring to intentional resourcing, where every person is motivated and empowered to do their best work from day one.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12257" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-1--1024x317.png" alt="Illustration of a stressed person with lightning bolts overhead, representing panic, paired with the text: Step 1 - Plan Before You Panic. Plan ahead to anticipate crunches and save time, money, and stress before fires start." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Stop waiting for the emergency to hit. Get ahead of the chaos.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We get it -  you’ve got a dozen fires burning already, and planning feels like a luxury. But trust us: spending a little time now beats the scramble (and overspending) later. Your future self will appreciate it.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12258" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-2-1024x318.png" alt="Step 2 of unlocking great work from freelance talent: Be brutally honest. Icon of a checklist and magnifying glass. Set clear expectations on role, responsibilities, hours, scope, and boundaries." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">No smoke. No mirrors. Just clarity.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tell talent exactly what they’re signing up for -  the good, the messy, and the non-negotiables. Clear scopes, realistic hours, and honest expectations build trust fast (and avoid awkward "that\'s not my job" convos later).</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12259" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-3-1024x317.png" alt="Step 3 is about onboarding freelance talent: Nail the onboarding. Icon of a hammer hitting a nail. Onboard early with clear briefs, brand guidelines, and context to ensure freelancers deliver from day one." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">This goes for freelancers and full-timers alike. Start early. Share org charts, “day-in-the-life” videos, brand guidelines - before they log a single hour. Add bulletproof briefs and a proper kick-off call so they can deliver on Day One instead of wandering through Week One in a fog.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12260" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-4-1024x318.png" alt="Step 4 is about empowering freelance talent: Build belonging and loyalty. Icon of hands stacked together. Include freelancers in meetings and communication to foster one aligned, loyal team." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Blended teams - part freelancers, part full-timers - are the new norm. Sure, there are legal lines you can’t cross, but that’s no excuse to treat freelancers like the B-team. Loop them into meetings, hold regular one-on-ones, keep them in the same comms channels. The goal? No “us vs. them,” just one team, same mission.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12261" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-5-1024x317.png" alt="Step 5 is about Understanding what motivates them. Icon of a flag atop a bar chart. Respect flexibility and autonomy, set expectations, and avoid scope creep to unlock their best work." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, the paycheck matters. But so does flexibility, autonomy, and meaningful work. Respect the boundaries in your contractor agreements, avoid scope creep, and skip the “one more tiny change” requests that aren’t in the brief. Freelancers thrive when their work is valued - give them room to ramp up, set clear expectations, and they’ll bring their best.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12262" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-6-1024x318.png" alt="Step 6 is about enabling freelance talent: Provide tools, context, and feedback. Icon of a tool bag. Equip freelancers with full access, training, goals, and open communication to help them succeed." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tools, training, and context aren’t “nice-to-haves” - they’re essentials.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Set them up with full access and the “why” behind your business. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Think:</span>\r\n\r\n<strong>- Transparent comms</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>- A go-to person for questions</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>- Inclusive team culture</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>- Clarity on how their work ladders up to the mission</strong>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12263" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-7-1024x317.png" alt="Step 7is about treating freelancers like trusted partners. Icon of two hands gripping in support. Delegate routine work so full-timers can focus on high-impact projects." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">You found great talent - now make the most of it. Offload the repeatable stuff so your internal team can focus on high-impact projects. It’s not about dumping tasks -  it’s about creating flow. The right freelancers amplify your in-house team’s superpowers.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<strong>Need a recap?</strong>\r\n\r\nIf you love a good checklist, here’s a quick-hit summary of the key steps to motivate and empower your flexible talent. From planning ahead to treating them like trusted partners, each step plays a role in making your flex team feel supported, aligned, and ready to deliver their best work.\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12274" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Quick-Reference-Table-v3-1024x1024.png" alt="Summary chart of seven steps to motivate and empower freelance talent. Includes planning, transparency, onboarding, inclusion, motivation, tools, and trusted partnerships." width="1024" height="1024" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">At Sandy, we build flexible, high-performing creative teams that slot right into your world - whether you’re running an in-house team, a hybrid setup, or or need a support team spun up yesterday.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re done with last-minute scrambles and want a partner who can hit the ground running with you, <a href="https://worksandy.com/find-talent/">let’s talk</a>.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ll help you scale smarter, move faster, and keep your team focused on the work that actually moves the needle.</span>', 'The Secret to Unlocking Great Work from Your Flexible Talent', '', 'publish', 'open', 'open', '', 'the-secret-to-unlocking-great-work-from-flexible-talent', '', '', '2025-08-15 13:48:33', '2025-08-15 17:48:33', '', 0, 'https://worksandy.com/?p=12256', 0, 'post', '', 0),
(12257, 5, '2025-08-14 18:47:06', '2025-08-14 22:47:06', 'The image features a purple-themed graphic split into two sections. On the left, a simplified outline of a person is shown with three lightning bolts above their head, symbolizing stress or overwhelm. Small plus signs and dots surround the figure, indicating a chaotic or urgent situation. On the right, bold text reads “Step 1: Plan Before You Panic,” followed by a supporting line: “Plan ahead to anticipate crunches and save time, money, and stress before fires start.” The design visually reinforces the need for proactive planning before burnout or team pressure sets in.', 'Step 1', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-1', '', '', '2025-08-14 18:53:25', '2025-08-14 22:53:25', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-1-.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12258, 5, '2025-08-14 19:10:10', '2025-08-14 23:10:10', 'A green-toned visual featuring two sections. On the left, an icon shows a clipboard with four checkboxes and a magnifying glass—symbolizing transparency, clarity, and attention to detail. On the right, the bolded text reads: “Step 2: Be Brutally Honest,” followed by the subtext: “State role, responsibilities, hours, scope, and boundaries up front to build trust and avoid surprises.”\nThis image supports the blog section focused on transparent freelancer onboarding and expectation setting—crucial for retaining top creative talent and reducing miscommunication.', 'Step 2', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-2', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:11:39', '2025-08-14 23:11:39', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-2.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12259, 5, '2025-08-14 19:12:19', '2025-08-14 23:12:19', 'A dark blue visual split into two sections. On the left is an outlined icon of a hammer driving a nail into a surface—symbolizing preparation, precision, and execution. On the right, white text reads: “Step 3: Nail the Onboarding,” with a supporting message: “Onboard early with context, guidelines, solid briefs, and a kickoff so they can deliver on Day One.”\nThe image visually emphasizes the importance of intentional, well-structured onboarding when working with freelance or contract talent, reinforcing the blog’s call to replace chaos with clarity.', 'Step 3', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-3', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:13:11', '2025-08-14 23:13:11', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-3.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12260, 5, '2025-08-14 19:13:50', '2025-08-14 23:13:50', 'A warm brown visual divided into two parts. On the left is a simple line illustration of three hands stacked on top of each other, representing unity, inclusion, and team alignment. On the right, white text reads: “Step 4: Build Belonging and Loyalty,” with a supporting sentence: “Include freelancers in meetings, comms, and 1:1s to create one aligned, loyal team.”\nThis image reinforces the blog’s emphasis on integrating freelancers into the fabric of your culture to drive loyalty, performance, and shared purpose.', 'Step 4', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-4', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:14:43', '2025-08-14 23:14:43', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-4.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12261, 5, '2025-08-14 19:15:15', '2025-08-14 23:15:15', 'A soft pink visual with two distinct sections. On the left, a minimalist icon shows a three-tiered bar chart with a flag planted at the top—symbolizing achievement, motivation, and progress. On the right, white text reads: “Step 5: Understand What Motivates Them,” followed by: “Respect flexibility and autonomy, set clear expectations, and prevent scope creep so they do their best work.”\nThe image visually supports the message that empowered freelancers thrive when their goals, boundaries, and motivation are clearly respected and aligned.', 'Step 5', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-5', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:16:23', '2025-08-14 23:16:23', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-5.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12262, 5, '2025-08-14 19:17:01', '2025-08-14 23:17:01', 'An olive green graphic divided into two halves. On the left, a line art icon shows a tool bag—representing access to essential resources, support, and preparation. On the right, white text reads: “Step 6: Give Them the Tools, Context, and Feedback,” with a supporting line: “Give full access, training, clear goals, and the \'why\'—plus transparent comms and a buddy—to help them excel.”\nThis visual reinforces the need for structured support, clarity, and connection to set up freelancers for success from day one.', 'Step 6', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-6', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:17:51', '2025-08-14 23:17:51', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-6.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12263, 5, '2025-08-14 19:19:05', '2025-08-14 23:19:05', 'A teal-colored graphic with two sections. On the left, a minimal icon shows two hands grasping each other in a firm, supportive grip—symbolizing trust, partnership, and collaboration. On the right, white text reads: “Step 7: Treat Them Like Trusted Partners,” followed by: “Delegate routine work to trusted freelancers so full-timers can focus on high-impact projects.”\nThis image supports the blog’s message of fostering trust, distributing work wisely, and valuing freelancers as strategic extensions of your core team.', 'Step 7', '', 'inherit', 'open', 'closed', '', 'step-7', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:20:07', '2025-08-14 23:20:07', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-7.png', 0, 'attachment', 'image/png', 0),
(12265, 5, '2025-08-14 19:37:33', '2025-08-14 23:37:33', '<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ve all been there.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The team’s underwater, deadlines are looming, and Slack has taken on a tone of panic. You know it’s time to bring in help - but by the time you do, things are already on fire.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">So you start scrambling - pinging old contacts, texting friends-of-friends, chasing down leads like your next deliverable depends on it (because, well, it does). You finally land someone great, rush through contracts, toss them an NDA, and then… throw them in the deep end.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s a familiar move: hiring out of urgency, not strategy. And while it might get you across the finish line, it rarely sets your new hire - or your team - up for long-term success.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The good news? There’s a better way. One that makes bringing in the right support faster, easier, and actually effective. Let’s talk about moving from reactive hiring to intentional resourcing, where every person is motivated and empowered to do their best work from day one.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12257" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-1--1024x317.png" alt="Illustration of a stressed person with lightning bolts overhead, representing panic, paired with the text: Step 1 - Plan Before You Panic. Plan ahead to anticipate crunches and save time, money, and stress before fires start." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Stop waiting for the emergency to hit. Get ahead of the chaos.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We get it -  you’ve got a dozen fires burning already, and planning feels like a luxury. But trust us: spending a little time now beats the scramble (and overspending) later. Your future self will appreciate it.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12258" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-2-1024x318.png" alt="Step 2 of unlocking great work from freelance talent: Be brutally honest. Icon of a checklist and magnifying glass. Set clear expectations on role, responsibilities, hours, scope, and boundaries." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">No smoke. No mirrors. Just clarity.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tell talent exactly what they’re signing up for -  the good, the messy, and the non-negotiables. Clear scopes, realistic hours, and honest expectations build trust fast (and avoid awkward "that\'s not my job" convos later).</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12259" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-3-1024x317.png" alt="Step 3 is about onboarding freelance talent: Nail the onboarding. Icon of a hammer hitting a nail. Onboard early with clear briefs, brand guidelines, and context to ensure freelancers deliver from day one." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">This goes for freelancers and full-timers alike. Start early. Share org charts, “day-in-the-life” videos, brand guidelines - before they log a single hour. Add bulletproof briefs and a proper kick-off call so they can deliver on Day One instead of wandering through Week One in a fog.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12260" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-4-1024x318.png" alt="Step 4 is about empowering freelance talent: Build belonging and loyalty. Icon of hands stacked together. Include freelancers in meetings and communication to foster one aligned, loyal team." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Blended teams - part freelancers, part full-timers - are the new norm. Sure, there are legal lines you can’t cross, but that’s no excuse to treat freelancers like the B-team. Loop them into meetings, hold regular one-on-ones, keep them in the same comms channels. The goal? No “us vs. them,” just one team, same mission.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12261" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-5-1024x317.png" alt="Step 5 is about Understanding what motivates them. Icon of a flag atop a bar chart. Respect flexibility and autonomy, set expectations, and avoid scope creep to unlock their best work." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, the paycheck matters. But so does flexibility, autonomy, and meaningful work. Respect the boundaries in your contractor agreements, avoid scope creep, and skip the “one more tiny change” requests that aren’t in the brief. Freelancers thrive when their work is valued - give them room to ramp up, set clear expectations, and they’ll bring their best.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12262" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-6-1024x318.png" alt="Step 6 is about enabling freelance talent: Provide tools, context, and feedback. Icon of a tool bag. Equip freelancers with full access, training, goals, and open communication to help them succeed." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tools, training, and context aren’t “nice-to-haves” - they’re essentials.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Set them up with full access and the “why” behind your business. Think:</span>\r\n\r\n<strong>Transparent comms</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>A go-to person for questions</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Inclusive team culture</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Clarity on how their work ladders up to the mission</strong>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12263" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-7-1024x317.png" alt="Step 7is about treating freelancers like trusted partners. Icon of two hands gripping in support. Delegate routine work so full-timers can focus on high-impact projects." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">You found great talent - now make the most of it. Offload the repeatable stuff so your internal team can focus on high-impact projects. It’s not about dumping tasks -  it’s about creating flow. The right freelancers amplify your in-house team’s superpowers.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12264" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Table-v3-1024x1024.png" alt="Summary chart of seven steps to motivate and empower freelance talent. Includes planning, transparency, onboarding, inclusion, motivation, tools, and trusted partnerships." width="1024" height="1024" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">At Sandy, we build flexible, high-performing creative teams that slot right into your world - whether you’re running an in-house team, a hybrid setup, or or need a support team spun up yesterday.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re done with last-minute scrambles and want a partner who can hit the ground running with you, <a href="https://worksandy.com/find-talent/">let’s talk</a>.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ll help you scale smarter, move faster, and keep your team focused on the work that actually moves the needle.</span>', 'The Secret to Unlocking Great Work from Your Flexible Talent', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '12256-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:37:33', '2025-08-14 23:37:33', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/?p=12265', 0, 'revision', '', 0) ;
INSERT INTO `ULhz1h_posts` ( `ID`, `post_author`, `post_date`, `post_date_gmt`, `post_content`, `post_title`, `post_excerpt`, `post_status`, `comment_status`, `ping_status`, `post_password`, `post_name`, `to_ping`, `pinged`, `post_modified`, `post_modified_gmt`, `post_content_filtered`, `post_parent`, `guid`, `menu_order`, `post_type`, `post_mime_type`, `comment_count`) VALUES
(12266, 5, '2025-08-14 19:38:31', '2025-08-14 23:38:31', '<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ve all been there.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The team’s underwater, deadlines are looming, and Slack has taken on a tone of panic. You know it’s time to bring in help - but by the time you do, things are already on fire.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">So you start scrambling - pinging old contacts, texting friends-of-friends, chasing down leads like your next deliverable depends on it (because, well, it does). You finally land someone great, rush through contracts, toss them an NDA, and then… throw them in the deep end.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s a familiar move: hiring out of urgency, not strategy. And while it might get you across the finish line, it rarely sets your new hire - or your team - up for long-term success.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The good news? There’s a better way. One that makes bringing in the right support faster, easier, and actually effective. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Let’s talk about moving from reactive hiring to intentional resourcing, where every person is motivated and empowered to do their best work from day one.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12257" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-1--1024x317.png" alt="Illustration of a stressed person with lightning bolts overhead, representing panic, paired with the text: Step 1 - Plan Before You Panic. Plan ahead to anticipate crunches and save time, money, and stress before fires start." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Stop waiting for the emergency to hit. Get ahead of the chaos.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We get it -  you’ve got a dozen fires burning already, and planning feels like a luxury. But trust us: spending a little time now beats the scramble (and overspending) later. Your future self will appreciate it.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12258" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-2-1024x318.png" alt="Step 2 of unlocking great work from freelance talent: Be brutally honest. Icon of a checklist and magnifying glass. Set clear expectations on role, responsibilities, hours, scope, and boundaries." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">No smoke. No mirrors. Just clarity.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tell talent exactly what they’re signing up for -  the good, the messy, and the non-negotiables. Clear scopes, realistic hours, and honest expectations build trust fast (and avoid awkward "that\'s not my job" convos later).</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12259" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-3-1024x317.png" alt="Step 3 is about onboarding freelance talent: Nail the onboarding. Icon of a hammer hitting a nail. Onboard early with clear briefs, brand guidelines, and context to ensure freelancers deliver from day one." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">This goes for freelancers and full-timers alike. Start early. Share org charts, “day-in-the-life” videos, brand guidelines - before they log a single hour. Add bulletproof briefs and a proper kick-off call so they can deliver on Day One instead of wandering through Week One in a fog.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12260" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-4-1024x318.png" alt="Step 4 is about empowering freelance talent: Build belonging and loyalty. Icon of hands stacked together. Include freelancers in meetings and communication to foster one aligned, loyal team." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Blended teams - part freelancers, part full-timers - are the new norm. Sure, there are legal lines you can’t cross, but that’s no excuse to treat freelancers like the B-team. Loop them into meetings, hold regular one-on-ones, keep them in the same comms channels. The goal? No “us vs. them,” just one team, same mission.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12261" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-5-1024x317.png" alt="Step 5 is about Understanding what motivates them. Icon of a flag atop a bar chart. Respect flexibility and autonomy, set expectations, and avoid scope creep to unlock their best work." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, the paycheck matters. But so does flexibility, autonomy, and meaningful work. Respect the boundaries in your contractor agreements, avoid scope creep, and skip the “one more tiny change” requests that aren’t in the brief. Freelancers thrive when their work is valued - give them room to ramp up, set clear expectations, and they’ll bring their best.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12262" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-6-1024x318.png" alt="Step 6 is about enabling freelance talent: Provide tools, context, and feedback. Icon of a tool bag. Equip freelancers with full access, training, goals, and open communication to help them succeed." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tools, training, and context aren’t “nice-to-haves” - they’re essentials.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Set them up with full access and the “why” behind your business. Think:</span>\r\n\r\n<strong>Transparent comms</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>A go-to person for questions</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Inclusive team culture</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Clarity on how their work ladders up to the mission</strong>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12263" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-7-1024x317.png" alt="Step 7is about treating freelancers like trusted partners. Icon of two hands gripping in support. Delegate routine work so full-timers can focus on high-impact projects." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">You found great talent - now make the most of it. Offload the repeatable stuff so your internal team can focus on high-impact projects. It’s not about dumping tasks -  it’s about creating flow. The right freelancers amplify your in-house team’s superpowers.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12264" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Table-v3-1024x1024.png" alt="Summary chart of seven steps to motivate and empower freelance talent. Includes planning, transparency, onboarding, inclusion, motivation, tools, and trusted partnerships." width="1024" height="1024" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">At Sandy, we build flexible, high-performing creative teams that slot right into your world - whether you’re running an in-house team, a hybrid setup, or or need a support team spun up yesterday.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re done with last-minute scrambles and want a partner who can hit the ground running with you, <a href="https://worksandy.com/find-talent/">let’s talk</a>.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ll help you scale smarter, move faster, and keep your team focused on the work that actually moves the needle.</span>', 'The Secret to Unlocking Great Work from Your Flexible Talent', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '12256-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:38:31', '2025-08-14 23:38:31', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/?p=12266', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
(12267, 5, '2025-08-14 19:38:52', '2025-08-14 23:38:52', '<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ve all been there.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The team’s underwater, deadlines are looming, and Slack has taken on a tone of panic. You know it’s time to bring in help - but by the time you do, things are already on fire.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">So you start scrambling - pinging old contacts, texting friends-of-friends, chasing down leads like your next deliverable depends on it (because, well, it does). You finally land someone great, rush through contracts, toss them an NDA, and then… throw them in the deep end.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">It’s a familiar move: hiring out of urgency, not strategy. And while it might get you across the finish line, it rarely sets your new hire - or your team - up for long-term success.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">The good news? There’s a better way. One that makes bringing in the right support faster, easier, and actually effective. </span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Let’s talk about moving from reactive hiring to intentional resourcing, where every person is motivated and empowered to do their best work from day one.</span>\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12257" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-1--1024x317.png" alt="Illustration of a stressed person with lightning bolts overhead, representing panic, paired with the text: Step 1 - Plan Before You Panic. Plan ahead to anticipate crunches and save time, money, and stress before fires start." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n&nbsp;\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Stop waiting for the emergency to hit. Get ahead of the chaos.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We get it -  you’ve got a dozen fires burning already, and planning feels like a luxury. But trust us: spending a little time now beats the scramble (and overspending) later. Your future self will appreciate it.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12258" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-2-1024x318.png" alt="Step 2 of unlocking great work from freelance talent: Be brutally honest. Icon of a checklist and magnifying glass. Set clear expectations on role, responsibilities, hours, scope, and boundaries." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">No smoke. No mirrors. Just clarity.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tell talent exactly what they’re signing up for -  the good, the messy, and the non-negotiables. Clear scopes, realistic hours, and honest expectations build trust fast (and avoid awkward "that\'s not my job" convos later).</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12259" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-3-1024x317.png" alt="Step 3 is about onboarding freelance talent: Nail the onboarding. Icon of a hammer hitting a nail. Onboard early with clear briefs, brand guidelines, and context to ensure freelancers deliver from day one." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">This goes for freelancers and full-timers alike. Start early. Share org charts, “day-in-the-life” videos, brand guidelines - before they log a single hour. Add bulletproof briefs and a proper kick-off call so they can deliver on Day One instead of wandering through Week One in a fog.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12260" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-4-1024x318.png" alt="Step 4 is about empowering freelance talent: Build belonging and loyalty. Icon of hands stacked together. Include freelancers in meetings and communication to foster one aligned, loyal team." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Blended teams - part freelancers, part full-timers - are the new norm. Sure, there are legal lines you can’t cross, but that’s no excuse to treat freelancers like the B-team. Loop them into meetings, hold regular one-on-ones, keep them in the same comms channels. The goal? No “us vs. them,” just one team, same mission.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12261" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-5-1024x317.png" alt="Step 5 is about Understanding what motivates them. Icon of a flag atop a bar chart. Respect flexibility and autonomy, set expectations, and avoid scope creep to unlock their best work." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Yes, the paycheck matters. But so does flexibility, autonomy, and meaningful work. Respect the boundaries in your contractor agreements, avoid scope creep, and skip the “one more tiny change” requests that aren’t in the brief. Freelancers thrive when their work is valued - give them room to ramp up, set clear expectations, and they’ll bring their best.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12262" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-6-1024x318.png" alt="Step 6 is about enabling freelance talent: Provide tools, context, and feedback. Icon of a tool bag. Equip freelancers with full access, training, goals, and open communication to help them succeed." width="1024" height="318" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Tools, training, and context aren’t “nice-to-haves” - they’re essentials.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">Set them up with full access and the “why” behind your business. Think:</span>\r\n\r\n<strong>Transparent comms</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>A go-to person for questions</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Inclusive team culture</strong>\r\n\r\n<strong>Clarity on how their work ladders up to the mission</strong>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12263" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Step-7-1024x317.png" alt="Step 7is about treating freelancers like trusted partners. Icon of two hands gripping in support. Delegate routine work so full-timers can focus on high-impact projects." width="1024" height="317" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">You found great talent - now make the most of it. Offload the repeatable stuff so your internal team can focus on high-impact projects. It’s not about dumping tasks -  it’s about creating flow. The right freelancers amplify your in-house team’s superpowers.</span>\r\n\r\n<img class="alignnone size-large wp-image-12264" src="https://worksandy.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/08/Table-v3-1024x1024.png" alt="Summary chart of seven steps to motivate and empower freelance talent. Includes planning, transparency, onboarding, inclusion, motivation, tools, and trusted partnerships." width="1024" height="1024" />\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">At Sandy, we build flexible, high-performing creative teams that slot right into your world - whether you’re running an in-house team, a hybrid setup, or or need a support team spun up yesterday.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">If you’re done with last-minute scrambles and want a partner who can hit the ground running with you, <a href="https://worksandy.com/find-talent/">let’s talk</a>.</span>\r\n\r\n<span style="font-weight: 400;">We’ll help you scale smarter, move faster, and keep your team focused on the work that actually moves the needle.</span>', 'The Secret to Unlocking Great Work from Your Flexible Talent', '', 'inherit', 'closed', 'closed', '', '12256-revision-v1', '', '', '2025-08-14 19:38:52', '2025-08-14 23:38:52', '', 12256, 'https://worksandy.com/?p=12267', 0, 'revision', '', 0),
